diet, monitor weight daily for fluid retention, and avoid excessive fluid intake. Encourage gradual resumption of physical activity as tolerated. Educate on recognizing signs of worsening heart failure, such as increased shortness of breath, swelling, or weight gain. 4. Follow-up: Schedule a follow-up appointment within one to two weeks for reassessment of symptoms, review of laboratory results, and adjustment of medications as needed. If symptoms worsen or new symptoms develop, seek immediate medical attention."
